canonical_claim.statement:
[Corrected statement, from the from-scratch check of the correction and the validators' repair] Proposition 1 (revised). Under Assumption 2, with $X_i = \theta_i Y_i$, $\delta_i = \mathrm{E}[X_i] - \beta$ and $b_n = \frac1n\delta^{\mathsf T}(I + A^{\mathcal O})\delta$:
(i) for any $\epsilon > 0$, $\lim_{n\to\infty}\Pr\left(\left|n\widehat V_1(A^{\mathcal O};Z) - n\,\mathrm{var}(\hat\beta) - b_n\right| > \epsilon\right) = 0$;
(ii) $\mathrm{E}[n\widehat V_1(A^{\mathcal O};Z)] = n\,\mathrm{var}(\hat\beta) + b_n + O(n^{-1})$; explicitly $\left|\mathrm{E}[n\widehat V_1(A^{\mathcal O};Z)] - n\,\mathrm{var}(\hat\beta) - b_n\right| \le \frac{3(1 + c_2)^2c_1^2}{n}$;
(iii) $\hat\sigma_\theta^2 - \frac1n\sum_{i}\mathrm{var}(X_i) - \frac1n\sum_i\delta_i^2 \to 0$ in probability (the limit of the plug-in sample variance includes the mean term $\frac1n\sum_i\delta_i^2$);
(iv) [consistency] the conclusion of the printed Proposition 1, $\lim_{n\to\infty}\Pr(|n\widehat V_1(A^{\mathcal O};Z) - n\,\mathrm{var}(\hat\beta)| > \epsilon) = 0$ for any $\epsilon > 0$, holds if and only if $b_n \to 0$. A sufficient condition is $\mathrm{E}[\theta_i Y_i] = \beta$ for every $i \in \mathcal V_S$ and every $n$ (then $\delta = 0$);
(v) [conservativeness of the oracle] $\lim_{n\to\infty}\Pr(n\,\mathrm{var}(\hat\beta) - n\widehat V_1(A^{\mathcal O};Z) > \epsilon) = 0$ for any $\epsilon > 0$ holds if and only if $\liminf_{n\to\infty} b_n \ge 0$. A sufficient condition is that $I + A^{\mathcal O}$ is positive semidefinite for every $n$;
(vi) [which graphs] for the adjacency matrix $A$ of a simple graph, $I + A$ is positive semidefinite if and only if the graph is a disjoint union of cliques; in that case $\widehat V_1(A;Z) = \frac{1}{n^2}\sum_{\text{cliques } c}\left(\sum_{i \in c} e_i\right)^2$ with $e_i = \theta_i Y_i - \hat\beta$.
The sentence of the printed proof "Asymptotic unbiasedness follows directly from linearity of expectations and $\mathrm{var}(\hat\beta) = O(n^{-1})$" (p. 2243) is replaced by (ii).

[Corrected statement, from the from-scratch check of the correction] Let $(M_n)$ be a deterministic sequence of symmetric $n \times n$ real matrices whose operator norms are bounded uniformly in $n$, $\|M_n\| \le K$, and let $\widehat V_{M_n} = \frac{1}{n^2}e^{\mathsf T}M_ne$ with $e_i = \theta_i Y_i - \hat\beta$. Under Assumption 2:
(i) [exact, each $n$] $\mathrm{E}[e^{\mathsf T}M_ne] = \mathrm{tr}(PM_nPC) + \delta^{\mathsf T}M_n\delta = \mathrm{tr}(M_nC) + \delta^{\mathsf T}M_n\delta - \frac{2}{n}1^{\mathsf T}M_nC1 + (1^{\mathsf T}M_n1)\,\mathrm{var}(\hat\beta)$, where $P = I - \frac1n 11^{\mathsf T}$;
(ii) $\mathrm{var}(e^{\mathsf T}M_ne) = O(n)$;
(iii) (F1) $n\widehat V_{M_n} - n\,\mathrm{var}(\hat\beta) - \frac1n\left[\mathrm{tr}\{(M_n - I - A^{\mathcal O})C\} + \delta^{\mathsf T}M_n\delta\right] \to 0$ in probability;
(iv) [sufficient condition] if in addition $M_n$ is positive semidefinite and $N_n := M_n - (I + A^{\mathcal O})$ is positive semidefinite for every $n$, then $\delta^{\mathsf T}M_n\delta \ge 0$ and $\mathrm{tr}(N_nC) \ge 0$, and therefore, for any $\epsilon > 0$ and whatever the unit means $\mathrm{E}[\theta_i Y_i]$, $\lim_{n\to\infty}\Pr(n\,\mathrm{var}(\hat\beta) - n\widehat V_{M_n} > \epsilon) = 0$. (The condition actually used on $N_n$ is $\mathrm{tr}(N_nC) \ge 0$ for every admissible covariance matrix $C$; only the diagonal entries of $N_n$ and its entries on the edges of $\mathcal G_S$ enter that trace.) The paper's choice $M_n = I + A^{\mathcal O}$ has $N_n = 0$ but is positive semidefinite only when $\mathcal G_S$ is a disjoint union of cliques (P011-T3 (vi));
(v) [the matrix must be deterministic] (iii) is false for a data-dependent matrix of bounded norm: let $X_1, \ldots, X_n$ be independent with $\Pr(X_i = 1) = \Pr(X_i = -1) = 1/2$ ($\theta_i = 1$, empty dependency graph, $C = I$, $\beta = 0$, $\delta = 0$) and $M = \frac1n XX^{\mathsf T}$, so that $\|M\| = 1$ and $\mathrm{tr}(M) = 1$. Then $n\widehat V_M = (1 - \hat\beta^2)^2 \to 1$ in probability and $n\widehat V_M - n\,\mathrm{var}(\hat\beta) \to 0$, whereas the bracket of (iii) is $\frac1n\mathrm{tr}\{(M - I)C\} = \frac{1 - n}{n} \to -1$. Graphs chosen by maximizing over the sample are therefore handled by domination in every sample (P011-T5 (c), P011-T7), not by (iii).

[Corrected statement, from the from-scratch check of the correction] Let $d_i' = \min\{d_i, n-1\}$, $t_i = 1 - 1/d_i'$ if $d_i' > 0$ and $t_i = 0$ if $d_i' = 0$, and $e_i = \theta_i Y_i - \hat\beta$. For $A \in \mathcal A(Z)$ define the degree-corrected estimator $\widehat V_1^{+}(A;Z) = \widehat V_1(A;Z) + \frac{1}{n^2}\sum_{i \in \mathcal V_S} t_i\,d_i^A\,e_i^2$ (F2), i.e. $\widehat V_{M_A}$ with $M_A = I + A + \mathrm{diag}(t_i d_i^A)$, and the closed-form bound $\widehat V_Y'(Z) = \frac{1}{n^2}\sum_{i \in \mathcal V_S}(1 + d_i')\,e_i^2$ (F3), i.e. $\widehat V_{I + D'}$. Let $A^{m+}$ be a maximizer of $\widehat V_1^{+}(A;Z)$ over $A \in \mathcal A(Z)$. Assume valid constraints ($\mathcal E_R \subseteq \mathcal E_S$, $d_i \ge \sum_j A^{\mathcal O}_{ij}$).
Finite statements, in every sample and for every $n$:
(a) for every $A \in \mathcal A(Z)$, $M_A = (D_A + A) + \mathrm{diag}(1 - d_i^A/d_i')$ (the ratio read as 0 when $d_i' = 0$), $x^{\mathsf T}(D_A + A)x = \sum_{i<j}A_{ij}(x_i + x_j)^2$ and $d_i^A \le d_i'$; hence $M_A$ is positive semidefinite and $\widehat V_1^{+}(A;Z) \ge 0$;
(b) $M_{A^{\mathcal O}} - (I + A^{\mathcal O}) = \mathrm{diag}(t_i d_i^{A^{\mathcal O}})$ is positive semidefinite, and $\|M_{A^{\mathcal O}}\| \le 1 + 2c_2$ under Assumption 2;
(c) $\widehat V_1^{+}(A^{m+};Z) \ge \widehat V_1^{+}(A^{\mathcal O};Z)$;
(d) $\widehat V_1^{+}(A;Z)$ is affine in $A$: with the weights $\hat v_{ij} = e_ie_j + \frac12\left(t_ie_i^2 + t_je_j^2\right)$, $i < j$, in program (3.6), and $w^\ast$ its optimal value, $n^2\widehat V_1^{+}(A^{m+};Z) = \sum_i e_i^2 + 2w^\ast$;
(e) $I + D'$ is positive semidefinite; $(I + D') - (I + A^{\mathcal O}) = (D' - D_{A^{\mathcal O}}) + (D_{A^{\mathcal O}} - A^{\mathcal O})$ with both terms positive semidefinite, where $x^{\mathsf T}(D_{A^{\mathcal O}} - A^{\mathcal O})x = \sum_{i<j}A^{\mathcal O}_{ij}(x_i - x_j)^2$; and $\widehat V_Y'(Z) \ge \widehat V_1(A;Z)$ for every $A \in \mathcal A(Z)$ (because $2e_ie_j \le e_i^2 + e_j^2$);
(f) if $d_i' = d'$ for every $i$, then $\widehat V_Y'(Z) = \widehat V_2'(Z) = \hat\sigma_\theta^2(1 + d')/n$;
(g) if $A$ is $d$-regular and $d_i' = D \ge 1$ for every $i$, then $\widehat V_1^{+}(A;Z) = \widehat V_1(A;Z) + d\left(1 - \frac1D\right)\frac{1}{n^2}\sum_i e_i^2$; in particular the added term is $(d - 1)\frac{1}{n^2}\sum_i e_i^2$ when $D = d \ge 1$, and $\widehat V_1^{+} = \widehat V_1$ when $d = 0$.
Asymptotic statement:
(h) under Assumption 2 and valid constraints, and for any unit means $\mathrm{E}[\theta_i Y_i]$, $\lim_{n\to\infty}\Pr(n\,\mathrm{var}(\hat\beta) - n\widehat V(Z) > \epsilon) = 0$ for any $\epsilon > 0$, where $\widehat V$ is any of $\widehat V_1^{+}(A^{\mathcal O};Z)$, $\widehat V_1^{+}(A^{m+};Z)$, $\widehat V_Y'(Z)$ and $\min\{\widehat V_1^{+}(A^{m+};Z), \widehat V_Y'(Z)\}$. No bound on the supplied degrees $d_i$ is needed beyond validity: Assumption 2's bound $c_2$ on the true degrees in $\mathcal G_S$ suffices;
(i) consequently, when every unit has the same degree bound $d'$, the paper's closed-form $\widehat V_2'(Z)$ of (3.9) satisfies the conclusion of (h) without Assumption 3.
